# Drug Classification using Decision Trees

## Overview
This project builds a Decision Tree Classifier to predict which drug (A, B, C, X, or Y) is appropriate for a patient, based on demographic and clinical features.

## Dataset
IBM Drug200 Dataset (drug200.csv)

## Technologies
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Scikit-learn
- Matplotlib

## Workflow
1. Load dataset
2. Data preprocessing (Label Encoding, missing value check)
3. Feature/target mapping and correlation analysis
4. Class distribution visualization
5. Train/Test split
6. Decision Tree training (criterion="entropy", max_depth=4)
7. Model evaluation
8. Tree visualization
9. Depth comparison (max_depth=3)

## Evaluation Metrics
- Accuracy Score

## Results
The model predicts the correct drug for a patient and visualizes the learned decision rules as a tree diagram.
